{
  "id": null,
  "uid": "hardware-health",
  "version": null,
  "title": "Hardware Health",
  "description": "The physical layer beneath the OS: temperature, thermal throttling, fans and power across the bare-metal fleet. Built to answer 'was that slowdown thermal?' after the fact, with a preventative glance row on top. kelpy is deliberately absent — it is a vpsAdminOS container with no hwmon, no thermal zones and no cooling devices, so a permanently grey column would teach nothing. Per-host drill-down lives on Host Drill-Down; this board exists for cross-host comparison. Disk and SSD wear is NOT here: see palimpsest#162.",
  "tags": ["fleet", "hardware"],
  "timezone": "browser",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "editable": true,
  "fiscalYearStartMonth": 0,
  "liveNow": false,
  "refresh": "1m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-24h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {},
  "weekStart": "",
  "annotations": {
    "list": []
  },
  "links": [],
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "datasource",
        "label": "Data source",
        "type": "datasource",
        "query": "prometheus",
        "refresh": 1,
        "hide": 0,
        "current": {},
        "options": [],
        "regex": "",
        "multi": false,
        "includeAll": false,
        "skipUrlSync": false
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Hosts throttling",
      "description": "Bare-metal hosts with at least one CPU/GPU cooling device stepped above 0 — the hardware declaring its own unhappiness, which compares across the fleet in a way an absolute temperature does not. Green at 0, amber at 1, red at 2+. GOTCHA: the type filter is a curated allowlist (Processor, cpufreq-*, devfreq-*, intel_powerclamp). Fans (pwm-fan, dell-smm-fan1) and sawtoothShark's TCC Offset are cooling devices too and sit permanently above 0 without any throttling happening — including them would make this tile read 3 at all times.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "count(max by (instance) (node_cooling_device_cur_state{type=~\"Processor|cpufreq.*|devfreq.*|intel_powerclamp\"}) > 0) or vector(0)",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": ""
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "#0ca30c",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "#fab219",
                "value": 1
              },
              {
                "color": "#d03b3b",
                "value": 2
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "wideLayout": true,
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Hottest sensor",
      "description": "The single warmest hwmon sensor anywhere on the bare-metal fleet, named by host and chip. Deliberately uncoloured: 50 °C on a Pi SoC and 63 °C on an Intel laptop core mean different things, so no absolute band is honest across this hardware. Read it for magnitude and for which machine, then take the verdict from the throttling tile.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "topk(1, max by (host, chip) (label_replace(node_hwmon_temp_celsius, \"host\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^.:]+).*\")))",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} {{chip}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "wideLayout": true,
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Closest to critical",
      "description": "Smallest gap between a sensor and its own published critical point, in °C — the one temperature reading that IS comparable across hardware. GOTCHA: node_hwmon_temp_crit_celsius is published by only two chips on this fleet, rk1b's NVMe (81.85 °C) and sawtoothShark's Intel cores (100 °C). The Pi SoC thermal zones publish no critical point at all, so rk1a and porcupineFish can never appear here however hot they get — this tile is a floor, not fleet coverage. Uncoloured for the same reason.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "bottomk(1, label_replace(node_hwmon_temp_crit_celsius - node_hwmon_temp_celsius, \"host\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^.:]+).*\"))",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} {{chip}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "decimals": 0,
          "mappings": [],
          "color": {
            "mode": "thresholds"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "value",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "justifyMode": "auto",
        "orientation": "auto",
        "textMode": "value_and_name",
        "wideLayout": true,
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": ["lastNotNull"],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 100,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Thermal",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Temperature by host",
      "description": "Warmest sensor per host over time, one line per machine, host colours matching Fleet Overview. This is the board's main forensic instrument: with the shared crosshair on, a spike that appears on one host alone is that machine's own load, while a spike across all of them is the room. Hosts appear only while they are reporting — the on-demand machines (sawtoothShark, stargazer, weedySeadragon, potbelliedSeahorse) leave gaps when powered off, which is expected and never a fault.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (host) (label_replace(node_hwmon_temp_celsius, \"host\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^.:]+).*\"))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisSoftMin": 20,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": [
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "porcupineFish"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#199e70"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "potbelliedSeahorse"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#c98500"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "rk1a"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#008300"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "rk1b"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#9085e9"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "sawtoothShark"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#e66767"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "stargazer"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#d55181"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "matcher": {
              "id": "byName",
              "options": "weedySeadragon"
            },
            "properties": [
              {
                "id": "color",
                "value": {
                  "mode": "fixed",
                  "fixedColor": "#d95926"
                }
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Temperature by sensor",
      "description": "The same temperatures broken out per chip, but curated down to the sensors that carry independent information: one representative SoC zone plus every non-SoC chip. This is where rk1b's NVMe can be compared against its SoC, and sawtoothShark's cores against its chassis sensor. GOTCHA: rk1a and rk1b each expose 7 thermal zones x 2 duplicate sensors — 14 series per host, all reading the same value. Pinning chip to thermal_zone0 and taking max by (host, chip) collapses that to one line per host without hiding anything real. palette-classic because the series set is host x chip and so depends on which hardware is present.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 5
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (host, chip) (label_replace(node_hwmon_temp_celsius{chip=~\"thermal_thermal_zone0|nvme.*|platform_.*\"}, \"host\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^.:]+).*\"))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} {{chip}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "celsius",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisSoftMin": 20,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 101,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Throttling",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 13
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Throttle state",
      "description": "Cooling-device step per host and device type. 0 means the device is not constraining anything; any value above 0 means the kernel is actively holding that CPU, GPU or package back for thermal reasons, and is the signal behind the glance tile. A flat band of zeroes is the healthy reading, drawn on a 0-1 axis so the step to 1 is unmissable; the axis grows on its own if a device steps higher. Same curated type allowlist as the tile — fans and TCC Offset are excluded because they sit above 0 permanently without indicating throttling. sawtoothShark's 8 per-core Processor devices are collapsed by max, so one line means any core throttling. palette-classic: the series set is host x device type.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (host, type) (label_replace(node_cooling_device_cur_state{type=~\"Processor|cpufreq.*|devfreq.*|intel_powerclamp\"}, \"host\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^.:]+).*\"))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} {{type}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 0,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "axisSoftMax": 1,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 102,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Cooling & power",
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 22
      },
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Fan speed",
      "description": "Measured fan RPM per host. Fans ramp before throttling starts, so a rising line here is the early warning the throttle panel has not fired yet. Do not read across hosts: the Pi pwm-fans idle near 200-300 RPM and sawtoothShark's Dell fan runs at thousands, so compare each line against its own history, not against its neighbours. palette-classic — series set is host x chip.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 23
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (host, chip) (label_replace(avg_over_time(node_hwmon_fan_rpm[10m]), \"host\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^.:]+).*\"))",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} {{chip}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "rotrpm",
          "decimals": 0,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 8,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Power draw",
      "description": "Watts, derived as volts x amps from the power-supply hwmon chips. GOTCHA: this exists at all only by accident of collector routing — sawtoothShark has the powersupplyclass collector explicitly disabled (d4cf95e), but the hwmon collector picks the same battery up as chip power_supply_bat0 and reports in0/curr1 regardless. The two sensors carry different sensor labels, hence the ignoring(sensor) join. Only sawtoothShark has a battery, so this panel is empty whenever that laptop is off, and the usbc source reads 0 W while running on battery. palette-classic — series set is host x chip.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 23
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "label_replace(node_hwmon_in_volts{chip=~\"power_supply.*\"} * ignoring(sensor) node_hwmon_curr_amps{chip=~\"power_supply.*\"}, \"host\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^.:]+).*\")",
          "range": true,
          "instant": false,
          "refId": "A",
          "legendFormat": "{{host}} {{chip}}"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "watt",
          "decimals": 2,
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "text",
                "value": null
              }
            ]
          },
          "custom": {
            "drawStyle": "line",
            "lineInterpolation": "smooth",
            "lineWidth": 2,
            "fillOpacity": 8,
            "showPoints": "never",
            "spanNulls": false,
            "gradientMode": "opacity",
            "pointSize": 5,
            "axisPlacement": "auto",
            "axisLabel": "",
            "axisSoftMin": 0,
            "scaleDistribution": {
              "type": "linear"
            },
            "stacking": {
              "mode": "none",
              "group": "A"
            },
            "hideFrom": {
              "legend": false,
              "tooltip": false,
              "viz": false
            }
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "options": {
        "legend": {
          "displayMode": "list",
          "placement": "bottom",
          "showLegend": true,
          "calcs": []
        },
        "tooltip": {
          "mode": "multi",
          "sort": "desc"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 9,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Cooling devices",
      "description": "Every cooling device the fleet exposes, including the fans and TCC Offset that the throttle panels deliberately exclude — so the exclusion is visible rather than silent. 'State' is the current step and 'Max' the highest step that device supports; a fan sitting at 1 of 1 is running normally, whereas a Processor device above 0 is throttling. Empty rows for a host mean it is powered off, not that it has no cooling.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "${datasource}"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 31
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (host, type) (label_replace(node_cooling_device_cur_state, \"host\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^.:]+).*\"))",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A",
          "format": "table"
        },
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "${datasource}"
          },
          "editorMode": "code",
          "expr": "max by (host, type) (label_replace(node_cooling_device_max_state, \"host\", \"$1\", \"instance\", \"([^.:]+).*\"))",
          "range": false,
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "B",
          "format": "table"
        }
      ],
      "transformations": [
        {
          "id": "merge",
          "options": {}
